                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 72-year-old male patient, admitted on 09/02/2019 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemia, chest X-ray showing hyperinflation without consolidation, and blood tests revealing mild inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously. Treatment consisted of nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, leading to satisfactory clinical improvement. The patient was discharged on 10/02/2019 in stable condition. We recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. Please do not hesitate to contact us if required.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
